chunk 1: 16 units, 34 patches applied (34 changes logged), 8 issues without patch, 0 patches failed
  MANUAL unit 1 [error] split / sota (sa + u + ta): The printed sota is sa + uta (sa uta). The draft splits it into sa + u + ta and glosses u "and" and ta "also"; ta is not a word. The note itself says "sa before uta", so draft and note disagree. Replace the two words u and ta by one word uta "also".
         suggested fix: sa + uta (uta = "also")
  MANUAL unit 2 [minor] hindi / जो झुकने योग्य और दूसरे थे: Hindi renders nantvā ("to be bent") plus anyā, English only "bent down the others"; the two translations disagree and Hindi is garbled. Align on one reading (nantvā is flagged unclear in the note).
         suggested fix: Make Hindi and English say the same thing about nantvā anyā, e.g. Hindi "जिसने बल से दूसरों को झुका दिया" if nantvā is left unrendered and noted.
  MANUAL unit 4 [minor] split / madhu-dhāram + abhi: The word abhi belongs to the token madhudhārama̱bhi (end of line a), but the draft lists it under the next token yamoja̱sātṛ̭ṇat; the token madhudhāram+abhi is therefore incomplete and the next token has an extra word. Move abhi to the earlier token and gloss it as the preverb of atṛṇat ("upon, over"), not "towards".
         suggested fix: move abhi to token madhudhārama̱bhi
  MANUAL unit 5 [error] gram / vayunā: vayunā is not an instrumental (inst. sg. would be vayunena); it is n. nom./acc. pl. of vayuna ("pattern, way, design"), and the relative yā (n. pl.) agrees with it: "which patterns Brahmaṇaspati made". The draft translation ("which Brahmaṇaspati made with insight") rests on a wrong case. No patch: gloss and both translations need a decision.
         suggested fix: vayunā n. acc. pl. "ways/designs"; English e.g. "the ways that Brahmaṇaspati made"
  MANUAL unit 5 [minor] split / duraḥ: duraḥ is part of the printed token śa̱radbhi̱rduro̭, but the draft puts it under the token varanta (and gives the token śaradbhirduro only śaradbhiḥ). Word-to-token assignment is shifted by one word.
         suggested fix: move duraḥ to token śa̱radbhi̱rduro̭
  MANUAL unit 5 [minor] english / those some beings: "those some beings" is ungrammatical and bhuvanā is glossed "beings, worlds" while the Hindi has भुवन (worlds).
         suggested fix: those several worlds that were to come to be (and gloss "worlds")
  MANUAL unit 7 [error] split / su + u (ṣo): The printed ṣo cannot come from su + u (that gives ṣū); it is saḥ + u (cf. sota in unit 1 of ch024): naki ṣo = nakiḥ ṣaḥ u asti. The draft invents su "indeed" + u "and".
         suggested fix: replace su+u by sa "he" + u "and"
  MANUAL unit 13 [minor] gram / vaśaḥ: "m. acc. sg." does not fit the form: the acc. sg. of vaśa is vaśam, and vaśaḥ is nom. sg. (or acc. pl.). Check against the printed text; no patch because the construction with anu is unsettled.
         suggested fix: m. nom. sg. (or acc. pl.)
